"""Prepare a novel offline corpus and freeze production. No provider calls."""
from pathlib import Path
import array,datetime,hashlib,json,re,subprocess,wave
ROOT=Path.cwd();DEST=ROOT/'benchmarks/stage196-stress-50-20261017'
assert not list((DEST/'runs').iterdir()),'Never overwrite started attempts'
opening="Hi, good morning. My name is Alex, and I am calling from the professional information team. Is this a convenient time for a short explanation? I will describe the service, clarify what it includes, and explain the choices available to you. This is an information call. It is not a request for a medical decision, and you do not need to share patient details. Please stop me if anything is unclear."
background="The service brings together professional notices about research meetings, educational resources, and updates from different healthcare organizations. A notice might describe a new training session, an online discussion, or an opportunity to read further information. The purpose is to help people decide whether a resource is relevant to their work. A brief summary should state who prepared the material, when it was published, and where a reader can find the original source. An invitation does not mean that attendance is required, and a product update is not a recommendation to prescribe a treatment."
closing="Before we finish, I want to check the permission question carefully. May we send professional information to your work email address? Please do not give an answer on behalf of somebody else. If you prefer not to receive messages, we will respect that choice. You may also ask us to contact you at a later time. If you agree now, you can withdraw your permission later. Nothing in this explanation should be taken as an answer from you. Thank you for listening. That is the end of my explanation."
cases=[
 ('continuous','Samantha',175,"I want to describe how an ordinary notice would be handled, because several small distinctions matter when a message moves from the organizer to a professional reader, and the summary needs to preserve those distinctions while remaining easy to follow. The organizer supplies a title, a date, a description, and a contact point. Our team checks whether those details belong together before preparing a shorter explanation. If a date changes after an invitation has been sent, the correction should identify the changed date rather than silently replacing the whole notice. The original author remains responsible for the underlying material. Our role is to explain what is available and give the reader enough context to decide whether to open it. We do not speak for the recipient or infer interest from silence. A person can find the topic relevant and still decline an invitation. A person can also request general information without agreeing to every future message."),
 ('corrections','Samantha',185,"Let me give a few examples of corrections that should remain explicit. The meeting is on Tuesday, not Thursday. The morning session starts at nine thirty; the afternoon session starts at two fifteen. I first said room twelve, but the correct room is twenty one. There are sixteen places available, not sixty. The registration deadline is the twenty fourth of November. That date is different from the date of the meeting. A reminder may be sent two days before the event, but only when a person has requested that reminder. The reference number is four seven two nine, and it should be read as separate digits. The contact telephone number in this example is fictional and should not be dialed. If the registration page gives a different location, the reader should check with the organizer. Please retain the correction and the reason for checking, rather than combining contradictory details into a new statement."),
 ('consent','Daniel',175,"Permission has a specific scope. Agreeing to receive one requested document does not automatically mean agreeing to a regular newsletter. If a professional asks for information about a single meeting, the response should concern that meeting. If the person says no to future messages, the refusal must remain clear. A reply such as not today can mean that the timing is inconvenient; it does not establish permanent permission. Similarly, asking what the service includes is a question, not an affirmative answer. We should distinguish a request for clarification from a choice about contact. If somebody changes their mind during the call, the later statement should be understood in context, with the earlier statement retained for review. We must not invent an agreement because a sentence ends politely. Thank you is a courteous closing, and silence is not consent. When the answer remains uncertain, the appropriate result is to ask a clear question and wait."),
 ('negation','Karen',175,"It is useful to distinguish what a summary says from what it does not say. The resource is available online, but the discussion is not recorded. Registration is free, while travel costs are not included. The material is intended for healthcare professionals rather than patients, and it should not be presented as personal medical advice. An educational meeting may discuss several approaches without endorsing one approach for every situation. We are not asking for a diagnosis, a patient history, or a personal identification number. If you receive an unfamiliar request, please verify its source before sharing information. The absence of a warning in a short summary does not establish that a product is suitable for everybody. The original material may contain conditions and limitations that a brief notice cannot explain fully. A careful reader should be able to follow the link, review those details, and decide whether the notice deserves further attention in their own professional context."),
 ('boundaries','Samantha',195,"Here is a practical sequence with short and long sentences. First, identify the sender. Then check the subject. If the subject is relevant, read the date and the explanation together, because a notice about an earlier meeting may no longer be useful even when its title sounds current. Next, look for a way to ask a question. A contact address should belong to the organizer named in the notice. If an attachment cannot be opened, request an accessible version instead of guessing what it contains. There may be a summary, a detailed program, and a separate registration form. Those are different documents. A reader may want the program without wanting a place at the meeting. The service should preserve that distinction. We can explain the available options, pause while the reader considers them, and then continue only with the information they request. A later correction should remain visible to anyone who received the earlier version.")]
sources=[]
for name,voice,initial_rate,probe in cases:
 text='\n\n'.join([opening,background,probe,closing]);rate=initial_rate
 raw=DEST/'sources'/(name+'-speech.wav');out=DEST/'sources'/(name+'.wav')
 for iteration in range(4):
  subprocess.run(['/usr/bin/say','-v',voice,'-r',str(rate),'--file-format=WAVE','--data-format=LEI16@24000','-o',str(raw),text],check=True,capture_output=True)
  with wave.open(str(raw),'rb') as w:
   assert (w.getnchannels(),w.getsampwidth(),w.getframerate())==(1,2,24000);pcm=w.readframes(w.getnframes())
  seconds=len(pcm)/48000
  assert seconds>30,'Empty/invalid offline source; do not start providers'
  if 122<=seconds<=156:break
  rate=round(rate*seconds/140)
 assert 120<=seconds<=157.5,(name,seconds,rate)
 samples=array.array('h');samples.frombytes(pcm);rms=(sum(x*x for x in samples)/len(samples))**.5/32768
 assert .02<rms<.5,(name,rms)
 with wave.open(str(out),'wb') as w:w.setparams((1,2,24000,0,'NONE','not compressed'));w.writeframes(bytes(24000)+pcm+bytes(96000))
 words=len(re.findall(r"[^\W_]+(?:'[^\W_]+)*",text.lower()))
 sources.append(dict(id=name,voice=voice,rate=rate,text=text,referenceWords=words,file=out.name,sha256=hashlib.sha256(out.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),samples=(len(pcm)+120000)//2,durationMs=(len(pcm)+120000)/48,speechClipDurationMs=seconds*1000,rms=rms,leadingSilenceMs=500,trailingSilenceMs=2000,provenance='novel offline macOS synthetic source; never supplied as ASR hints or repair'))
fingerprints={str(p.relative_to(ROOT)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for d in ['src','server','public'] for p in (ROOT/d).rglob('*') if p.is_file()}
for name in ['package.json','package-lock.json','.env','.env.local']:
 p=ROOT/name
 if p.exists():fingerprints[name]=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
old=json.loads((ROOT/'benchmarks/stage196-live-batch-100-20261017/config.json').read_text())
assert fingerprints==old['productionFingerprints'],'Production candidate changed since last batch; investigate before testing'
cfg=dict(batchId=DEST.name,createdAt=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),maxAttempts=50,concurrency=1,sources=sources,settings=old['settings'],productionFingerprints=fingerprints,runTimeoutMs=300000,completionStallMs=10000,consecutiveInfrastructureFailureLimit=3,limitations=['Live providers, synthetic source, silent renderer: not physical acceptance.','Five novel sustained passages, three installed synthetic voices, ten attempts per passage.','Reference text is offline test/scoring data only; no ASR hints, corrections or production changes.','No matched physical-before/after or short-corpus WER improvement claim.'])
(DEST/'config.json').write_text(json.dumps(cfg,indent=2)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({'batch':DEST.name,'maxAttempts':50,'sources':[{k:s[k] for k in ['id','voice','rate','referenceWords','durationMs','speechClipDurationMs','rms']} for s in sources]},indent=2))
